'''''Phillyrea latifolia''''', commonly known as '''green olive tree''' or '''mock privet''', is a species of tree in the family [[Oleaceae]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Flora Europaea Search Results |url=https://rbg-web2.rbge.org.uk/cgi-bin/nph-readbtree.pl/feout?FAMILY_XREF=&GENUS_XREF=Phillyrea&SPECIES_XREF=&TAXON_NAME_XREF=&RANK= |website=Flora Europaea |access-date=28 March 2020}}</ref> It is native to the [[Mediterranean Basin]], from [[Morocco]] and [[Portugal]] in the west, to the [[Levant]] in the east.<ref>{{cite web |title=''Phillyrea latifolia'' |url=http://www.floraiberica.es/floraiberica/texto/pdfs/11_133_02_Phillyrea.pdf |publisher=[[Flora Iberica]] |access-date=9 June 2021 |pages=3–5}}</ref>

